Summary: Don't deadlock when a window's OpenGL context is updated from the main thread
Category: graphics
Kind: fix
Origin: wine-mac-builds
From: written for wine-mac-builds
Source: none published
Upstream: no
Why: macdrv_update_opengl_context updates the context through
 OnMainThread, which queues the block on the main thread's run loop and
 waits for it. OnMainThread doesn't check whether it's already on the main
 thread, and the content view's viewWillDraw calls macdrv_update_opengl_context
 on the main thread for GL contexts added while the view wasn't on screen.
 The block then waits behind the main thread itself, and the main thread
 hangs for good, with every other thread that needs it (wined3d's command
 stream thread in wglSwapBuffers, for one). Update the context directly
 when already on the main thread. Upstream winemac has the same code in
 10.0 and 11.x.
 Seen in White Wolf Queen (Big Fish trial, Direct3D on OpenGL): on macOS 26
 it hung in 2 of 4 launches as its window went into its fullscreen Space.
Evidence: samples of the hung game (Second Chance integration run on
 meeka, 2026-11-16, 11.22-build4, six samples over 3 minutes, all the
 same): main thread in -[_NSEnterFullScreenTransitionController
 _doSucceededToEnterFullScreen] -> CA::Transaction::commit ->
 -[WineContentView viewWillDraw] -> macdrv_update_opengl_context ->
 OnMainThread -> dispatch_semaphore_wait; wined3d_cs thread in
 wglSwapBuffers -> framebuffer_surface_swap -> macdrv_context_activate ->
 macdrv_add_view_opengl_context -> OnMainThread, waiting for the main
 thread.
Applies to: wine 11.22 (macfixes, after 0057)
Status: built in macfixes-11.22-build5 (2026-11-17); the regression suite
 passes on it. Not yet confirmed with White Wolf.

diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_opengl.m b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_opengl.m
index c15aefe..5488840 100644
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_opengl.m
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_opengl.m
@@ -308,6 +308,13 @@ void macdrv_update_opengl_context(WineOpenGLContext *context)
                 [context clearDrawableLeavingSurfaceOnScreen];
                 context.view = view;
             }
+            else if ([NSThread isMainThread])
+            {
+                /* From the content view's viewWillDraw, which runs on the main
+                 * thread: OnMainThread would queue the block behind itself and
+                 * wait for ever. */
+                [context update];
+            }
             else OnMainThread(^{
                 [context update];
             });
